I did not add the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause is its entire authority, and it grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`. An HTTP import would exceed that grant, and the approval isn't reflected in the graph's declared capabilities. Also, `RunInfo` has no text field, so there's no "input's text" to put in the query. The `with` clause would need to add an HTTP client scoped to `metadata.internal.example`, and the input would need to carry the text, before this can be wired in.

The key `"urls"` and the newline-separated format are my assumptions, since the spec doesn't define the stored value.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = match state_read::get("urls") {
            Some(raw) => raw
                .lines()
                .map(str::trim)
                .filter(|line| !line.is_empty())
                .map(String::from)
                .collect(),
            None => Vec::new(),
        };
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

